<title>SINGAPORE: India sells Apr Bombay naphtha to Itochu at -$18/T.</title>
<headline>India sells Apr Bombay naphtha to Itochu at -$18/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has sold by tender 30,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) to Japanese trader Itochu at $18.00 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, free-on-board (fob) Bombay on the west coast, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender which offered the mid-April lifting cargo, closed on April 3 and was valid until April 4.</p>
<p>IOC's last LAN cargo from Bombay lifting February 20-22 was awarded at $23.00 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, fob.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
